  <p>The fixed-nuclei problem is still a coupled many-electron problem, and its admissible state must also respect the exchange symmetry of identical electrons. Can one-particle orbitals be assembled into a tractable fermionic state without pretending that the interaction is gone? That unresolved question starts Part II.</p>

